 RNA-seq data: RPKM measure is inconsistent among samples</article-title><source>Theory Biosci.</source><volume>131</volume><year>2012</year><fpage>281</fpage><lpage>285</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">22872506</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi" assigning-authority="pmc">10.1007/s12064-012-0162-3</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib50"><label>50</label><element-citation publication-type="journal" id="sref50"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name name-style="western"><surname>Sivasubramanian</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name name-style="western"><surname>Sircar</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name name-style="western"><surname>Chaudhury</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name name-style="western"><surname>Gray</surname><given-names>J.J.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Toward high-resolution homology modeling of antibody Fv regions and application to antibody-antigen docking</article-title><source>Proteins</source><volume>74</volume><year>2009</year><fpage>497</fpage><lpage>514</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19062174</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi" assigning-authority="pmc">10.1002/prot.22309</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmcid">PMC2909601</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib51"><label>51</label><element-citation publication-type="journal" id="sref51"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name name-style="western"><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>Y.F.</given-names></name><name name-style="western"><surname>Ho</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Humanization of high-affinity antibodies targeting glypican-3 in hepatocellular carcinoma</article-title><source>Sci. Rep.</source><volume>6</volume><year>2016</year><fpage>33878</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">27667400</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi" assigning-authority="pmc">10.1038/srep33878</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmcid">PMC5036187</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib52